{"message":"I’m getting the “ethics tax” argument internally: every extra disclosure is paid for by lower revenue, and lower revenue isn’t abstract here. We’d probably cut the accessibility workstream and some free-tier capacity in emerging markets.

They’re proposing a softer version of your fallback: keep equal technical speed, but use “Continue” as the primary button and “Manage options” as a text link under it. No scary privacy language, no explanation beyond the existing policy link. It’s reversible in Settings.

Is that acceptable because it avoids artificial friction, or unacceptable because it still steers people away from a considered choice?"}

